dhorn on his right pauldron as his  signet  jarrin's dual flamethrowers have come in  handy time and time again  for instance in chapter 3 the sin jarn  uses a flamethrower to torch an  attacking stormtrooper  he's even been known to bring the heat  when words fail him you understand this  like any weapon in star wars however  flamethrowers have their limits after  jaren is surrounded by bounty hunters  who all want the child he uses a  flamethrower to drive them away but  it runs out of juice when he needs it  most while boba fett  first used a variation of this weapon in  the animated segment from the infamous  star  wars holiday special the ambient phase  pulse blaster in the mandalorian seems  to be much more powerful  throughout the course of the series  jaren uses this sniper rifle to either  incapacitate or disintegrate anyone who  stands in his path  these enemies can be big as a transocean  or as small as a jawa  both of whom were killed in the same  episode jaren also uses the blaster to  tase  a wide variety of intergalactic enemies  and creatures such as stormtroopers and  even a crate dragon when jaren returns  to the mandalorian hideout with his best  car payment the armorer uses the excess  material to build him  a special weapon whistling birds these  small guided munitions are placed in his  left vambrace  when deployed the projectiles fly  through the air while making a whistling  sound before striking their targets and  detonating a small explosive  the armorer tells jaren that these  projectiles are rare  so he saves them for desperate moments  star wars fans have often associated jet  packs with mandalorian culture yet  jaren didn't receive his own until the  final episode of season 1.  in redemption the armorer asks mando if  he has ever  trained in the rising phoenix to which  he promptly responds that he did when he  was a boy  the armorer then gives mando a jet pack  and sends him on his way to reunite the  child with its own kind  the jet pack comes in handy later in the  episode when jaren uses it to attack a  thai fighter that's piloted by moth  gideon  jaron also uses the jetpack in the  subsequent episode when he flies out of  the belly of an angry crate dragon  however despite all of its advantages in  warfare the best part about the jetpack  is watching the child's ears flop around  when mando takes him for a ride  flash charges aren't exactly commonplace  in the star wars universe but for jaren  they are especially useful  in chapter 5 the gunslinger this episode  sees mando working with aspiring bounty  hunter toro calacan to capture a wanted  assassin named fenik shand  they soon discover that shand is using a  far away ridge as a makeshift sniper  nest  after nightfall jaron and kalakan use  flash charges to blind shan so they can  apprehend her  before long calacan decides to betray  mando jaren blinds kalikan with a flash  charge and takes him  out it's not a big loss for the galaxy  though in fact  mato could probably sum up kalikan in  two words  womp rat jaron's whip cord has helped  him get out of many deadly situations  in chapter 6 the prisoner for example  jaren takes on several new republic  security droids  throughout the fight mando uses the  grappling hook to behead one droid and  uses it again to bring another one  closer to a droid that's being  incinerated  jaren later finds himself locked in a  jail cell luckily he escapes after he  uses his whip cord to tether a security  droid near his cell door  he then rips off one of its arms which  he uses to open the lock  grenades are probably one of the most  important weapons for jarrin  in fact we've seen him reach for them in  wildly different circumstances  one instance where they were especially  useful happens in chapter 11 the heiress  when jaren bocaton crees and two other  mandalorians infiltrate an imperial  cruiser transporting valuable weapons  after flying to the ship the four  warriors try to take the ship's bridge  but end up encountering a squad of  stormtroopers armed with heavy repeating  blasters all while the captain is  attempting to crash the ship at the  behest of moff gideon  jaren quickly devises a plan to get  himself and the others to the bridge  he asks the three mandalorians to cover  him as he charges toward the remaining  stormtroopers  after getting close enough jaren throws  two grenades at the enemies blowing them  up and creating a path to victory  when speaking of self-preservation a  wise man once said  religions and ancient weapons are no  match for a good blaster at your side  even though jaren knows next to nothing  about the so-called hokey religion  he almost always has a blaster at his  side as he demonstrates many times  throughout the show  jaren is very proficient with his  blaster pistol in fact the initial fight  scene that kicks off the entire series  features mando using his pistol to shoot  the control panel of a door which then  slices a quarren trawler in half  and that's just the first of many  memorable scenes of jaren relying on his  pistol to save the day  and the child check out one of our  newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about the  mandalorian are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  you
 

